<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Milprop income edges up at half year.</title>
<headline>Milprop income edges up at half year.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net rental income     8.64	  vs 8.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-interest 9.59	  vs 9.85</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   4.12	  vs 4.70</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.95	  vs 0.88</p>
<p>    Turnover		  13.91	 vs 12.89</p>
<p>    Distributable income  5.46	  vs 5.16</p>
<p>Full name: Millennium Property Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The comparative figures are proforma. The group said it was paying an interim interest payment of 12.58 cents a debenture.</p>
<p>The group said the portfolio of properties continued to trade well and a reduction in repairs and maintenance in the second half should boost net rental income for the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
